course: dictionary
lesson: 9037
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Many words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which meaning the writer means. The word slate is a good example. «which left no mark on the slate» tells you the slate is something you write on, because a pencil leaves a mark on it.
explain: «a loose slate (a flat stone tile of the roof) falls with a crash» tells you a different meaning. The roof and the flat stone tile are the clues, so here slate means a thin piece of rock that covers a roof.
explain: Always check by swapping your meaning into the sentence. Does "a loose rock tile of the roof falls with a crash" still make sense? Yes, so the rock meaning fits.
fact: Slate is a hard, dark grey rock that splits into thin, flat sheets.
fact: A slate can be a thin piece of this rock used to cover a roof, or a small board that children wrote on with chalk in the past.
fact: A slate can also be a list of candidates or a plan, as in «a slate of films».
fact: To slate something (UK, informal) means to criticise it harshly, and «a clean slate» means a fresh start with past mistakes forgotten.
fact: Slate forms when shale is changed by pressure, which is why it splits into flat sheets.
exercise: «a loose slate (a flat stone tile of the roof) falls with a crash» What is a slate here? | A list of films | A dark grey cloud | *A thin flat piece of rock used to cover a roof | A small pencil
exercise: Ben says, "The critic slated the film in her review." What does slated mean? | Planned it for next year | Praised it warmly | Forgot all about it | *Criticised it harshly
exercise: Which phrase means a fresh start with past mistakes forgotten? | Loose slate | A slate of films | *A clean slate | Shale
test: Shale changed by pressure becomes which rock? | Marble | Chalk | Limestone | *Slate
test: «which left no mark on the slate» suggests what about the slate? | It was a broken roof tile | It was a long list of names | It was painted bright red | *It was a surface where a pencil could not write
exam: Which meaning of slate fits «The jurors in the book write their names on slates»? | *A small board for writing on with chalk | To criticise something harshly | A thin rock for covering a roof | A list of candidates
